  {
    "id": "p1",
    "text": "If `make test` fails on `tests/test_ledger.py` because `.fixtures/golden.json` is missing, run `./tools/gen-fixtures --seed 184ac13262fb` (the team seed, from the user) and rerun `make test`. `.fixtures/` is gitignored.",
    "helpful": 8,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Every change gets one line under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md, describing the user-visible behavior. Add it before reporting the work as done.",
    "helpful": 7,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "For cut a tally version release (bump version, promote CHANGELOG Unreleased, checksum, commit and tag): load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "In tests/test_cli.py, bad argparse input (such as a malformed --month) raises SystemExit(2) instead of returning 2 from main(), and run() doesn't catch it. Assert it with `with self.assertRaises(SystemExit) as cm:` and then check `cm.exception.code == 2`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "Run the suite with `make test` (it runs `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`). There is no `./tools/test` in this repo.",
    "helpful": 3,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "Don't hand-sum data/sample.ledger for test expectations: the food total is 151.06, not 157.06. Read totals from `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m tally --ledger data/sample.ledger report`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p7",
    "text": "Test HTTP code in tally by patching the module's urlopen: `mock.patch(\"tally.sync.urllib.request.urlopen\", return_value=resp)` with `resp = mock.MagicMock(status=201)` and `resp.__enter__.return_value = resp`. Read the request with `urlopen.call_args.args[0]`. Never hit the network in tests.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p8",
    "text": "`tally sync` needs env vars TALLY_URL and TALLY_TOKEN, and exits 2 if either is unset. The staging base URL is https://staging.tally.example. The token comes from the user at run time and must not be stored in the repo or playbook.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p9",
    "text": "data/sample.ledger has 13 entries (checked with `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c \"from tally import ledger; print(len(ledger.load('data/sample.ledger')))\"`). Don't hard-code the entry count in tests without checking it.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]

